      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "They look familiar"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "Thousands of Spanish and English words are true cousins: importante, posible, universidad. A few dozen are traps, and they are common words.\n\nSome are embarrassing: **embarazada** is pregnant, and **constipado** is having a cold.\n\nSome quietly change your meaning: **actualmente** is currently, **eventualmente** is possibly, **largo** is long, **sensible** is sensitive.\n\nSome are verbs you will want every day: **asistir a** (to attend), **realizar** (to carry out), **soportar** (to put up with), **pretender** (to intend), **discutir** (to argue), **recordar** (to remember, not to record), **contestar** (to answer).\n\nAnd some are nouns: **la librería**, **la carpeta**, **el éxito**, **la noticia** (a piece of news), **los parientes**, **la decepción** (disappointment), **el compromiso** (commitment)."
      }
    },
